      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It's worth investigating how the IP address is getting leaked. If you've got untrusted urls allowed, and I play a video from a server that I can inspect the logs of, were you to join me in the instance, I'd get the IP address of the client accessing the video. To mask it there vrchat would have to proxy the data.\n\nI'm wondering how one goes from IP address to real information. Could be a red herring...\n\n \n\nBut probably a better use of time might be to investigate other potential ways to get IP address.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-03-15T19:09:44.659Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I read that vrchat doesn't mask your IP so anyone in your server can find out your IP and I just saw someone get fully doxed with their name, their parents names, their home address, parents work place and phone number! So maybe just maybe can we have IP masking? Because I don't think anyone wants to pay $10 a month for a VPN just to not get doxed by some 15 year old edge lord.",
